WEBVTT

00:04.963 --> 00:06.297
<i>And then, guess what?</i>

00:06.381 --> 00:08.466
<i>Even though they'd</i>
<i>just had the hugest fight,</i>

00:08.550 --> 00:11.803
<i>apparently they started dating</i>
<i>the very next day!</i>

00:11.886 --> 00:14.055
Are you kidding me?

00:14.139 --> 00:18.018
<i>Ever since then, it's been called</i>
<i>the Matchmaking Ferris Wheel,</i>

00:18.101 --> 00:20.854
<i>and they say that if a couple</i>
<i>watches a sunset together from it,</i>

00:20.937 --> 00:22.981
<i>-they'll be happy together!</i>
<i>-</i>Uh?

00:23.064 --> 00:25.233
<i>On our next day off,</i>

00:25.316 --> 00:28.486
<i>I'd love to spend the day with you</i>
<i>and ride that Ferris wheel!</i>

00:28.570 --> 00:29.571
<i>I mean, if you want...</i>

00:30.613 --> 00:32.699
<i>Hello? Taiyo?</i>

00:32.782 --> 00:33.783
<i>Are you still there?</i>

00:33.867 --> 00:36.703
-Sorry, Mutsumi. I'm hanging up for now.
<i>-</i><i>What?</i>

00:39.706 --> 00:42.375
You're Taiyo Asano... Am I right?

00:42.459 --> 00:44.044
Uh, yes.

00:49.424 --> 00:52.510
I'm Hotokeyama of the Koizumi Precinct.

00:52.594 --> 00:53.845
POLICE OFFICER
SEIJI HOTOKEYAMA

00:53.928 --> 00:55.680
Would you mind coming with me?

01:04.773 --> 01:11.488
MISSION: YOZAKURA FAMILY

02:28.022 --> 02:30.400
KOIZUMI POLICE STATION

02:30.483 --> 02:32.443
-
Why don't we

02:32.527 --> 02:33.945
cut right to the chase, then?

02:34.028 --> 02:36.072
PLAN 5
INTERROGATION/DATE

02:36.656 --> 02:39.826
This was posted on the dark web.

02:40.952 --> 02:42.996
This is you, right?

02:43.079 --> 02:46.040
<i>Whoa, it's all over the Internet!</i>

02:46.124 --> 02:49.961
<i>But they told me that they covered up</i>
<i>all of the Yozakura family's activities!</i>

02:50.545 --> 02:52.297
Also...

02:53.381 --> 02:55.133
<i>possession and use of a firearm,</i>

02:55.216 --> 02:57.677
<i>trespassing onto private property...</i>

02:58.219 --> 03:00.763
<i>taking part in an early-morning car chase</i>
<i>on a public street.</i>

03:01.472 --> 03:04.142
<i>Ah... And you blew up your school, too?</i>

03:04.893 --> 03:08.229
I mean, are you trying
to become the god of juvenile crime?

03:08.313 --> 03:10.732
<i>Things I didn't do</i>
<i>are mixed up in there!</i>

03:11.357 --> 03:13.985
But you know
what's strange about this?

03:14.068 --> 03:16.905
There's nothing whatsoever
on your co-conspirators.

03:17.780 --> 03:21.201
Even though these are all crimes
that are clearly beyond kid territory.

03:21.284 --> 03:24.996
There's got to be more to this. Like...

03:25.079 --> 03:29.167
for reasons unknown, you belong
to some secret organization... maybe?

03:30.251 --> 03:33.504
If you have a good reason, you'll
get off easy on extenuating circumstances.

03:34.005 --> 03:36.799
If you know something,
you'd better start talking.

03:38.593 --> 03:41.846
<i>He's telling me</i>
<i>to sell everyone out?</i>

03:43.431 --> 03:45.266
I don't know anything!

03:45.808 --> 03:48.811
Well, hey, don't jump to conclusions.

03:49.979 --> 03:52.857
Have some water,
and give it a good, long think.

03:55.735 --> 03:58.321
<i>What? He just blatantly</i>
<i>poured something in there, right?</i>

03:59.572 --> 04:01.241
-Truth serum!
-Hmm?

04:01.950 --> 04:04.535
No, see, these are... minerals...

04:04.619 --> 04:06.996
that are good for you...

04:07.080 --> 04:08.289
<i>What a half-assed lie!</i>

04:08.373 --> 04:10.291
Just drink it like a good boy.

04:15.838 --> 04:18.716
WATER CATCHER THROAT BALLOON
FOR MAGIC TRICKS AND DRINKING GAMES

04:19.550 --> 04:22.095
I told you... I don't know anything!

04:22.595 --> 04:23.846
Is that right?

04:34.524 --> 04:38.695
That's a drug dealer who's
ruined the lives of thousands of people.

04:38.778 --> 04:40.905
Making full use
of his cash and connections,

04:40.989 --> 04:43.199
he'd been evading the law all this time...

04:43.783 --> 04:45.159
But I brought him to justice.

04:47.662 --> 04:51.541
It's not my job as a lawman
to protect those who break the law.

04:51.624 --> 04:55.461
<i>Is this guy really a cop?</i>

04:55.878 --> 05:01.426
If you won't give it up, I'll have to ask
your friends at school in person.

05:02.010 --> 05:03.386
<i>Damn this guy...</i>

05:06.723 --> 05:07.974
<i>I get it now!</i>

05:09.392 --> 05:13.563
I don't know anything,
but even if I did...

05:14.439 --> 05:17.984
I wouldn't give it up to a lunatic
like you if my life depended on it!

05:18.067 --> 05:19.861
I like that look
in your eyes.

05:19.944 --> 05:21.487
How many blows until they glaze over?

05:22.280 --> 05:23.489
Can't wait to find out.

05:31.205 --> 05:35.918
Oh my. Any further
and my suit would've been a mess!

05:36.002 --> 05:38.713
Aww... The jig is up, huh?

05:38.796 --> 05:39.881
It is indeed.

05:40.465 --> 05:44.093
"Ask your friends," when you're
digging for those friends' info?

05:44.844 --> 05:46.095
Who does that?

05:46.179 --> 05:49.349
You're as hopeless a liar as ever, Seiji.

05:49.432 --> 05:52.310
Shut the hell up.
That was my way of giving him a hint.

05:53.019 --> 05:55.521
Um... An explanation, please?

05:56.564 --> 05:59.233
He was a classmate
of mine in junior high.

05:59.317 --> 06:01.652
His name is Seiji Hotokeyama.

06:02.153 --> 06:04.447
Get your hands off me.
You'll give me a rash.

06:04.864 --> 06:07.450
In exchange for helping him
with his police investigations,

06:07.533 --> 06:10.787
we have him cover up
the Yozakura family's activities.

06:10.870 --> 06:14.415
Jeez. You're still
the same old piece of work.

06:14.957 --> 06:16.793
First you ambush me.

06:16.876 --> 06:21.297
Then you tell me that you're adding
your new kid brother to the mission.

06:21.381 --> 06:24.675
-Isn't more manpower a good thing?
-I guess.

06:25.385 --> 06:27.387
And how did he do?

06:27.970 --> 06:29.263
Let's see.

06:33.476 --> 06:39.065
You didn't sell out your allies,
and you didn't fall for my taunts.

06:39.607 --> 06:43.277
You pass.
Looking forward to working with you.

06:43.778 --> 06:45.071
R-Right.

06:45.571 --> 06:47.490
<i>Was that a smile?</i>

06:47.573 --> 06:49.742
Great! This is great!

06:50.701 --> 06:52.203
Feel free to run him ragged!

06:52.662 --> 06:58.126
Right. While you're here, I have
a big job for you in return for my help--

06:58.209 --> 07:01.504
Whoops, time for my next mission.

07:01.587 --> 07:03.047
I'll be heading out now!

07:03.131 --> 07:04.132
H-Hey!

07:04.590 --> 07:06.509
And you run along to school!

07:07.176 --> 07:08.761
W-Wait a sec!

07:13.057 --> 07:14.350
Can I give you a lift?

07:14.434 --> 07:16.519
No. I'll be fine.

07:22.692 --> 07:24.610
Taiyo, are you all right?

07:24.694 --> 07:27.071
Yeah... I'm fine.

07:27.155 --> 07:28.739
What happened?

07:28.823 --> 07:31.742
Uh, yeah... Just a...

07:31.826 --> 07:34.537
All right,
everyone, have a seat!

07:35.079 --> 07:36.831
Huh? That's Vice-Principal Hirukawa.

07:36.914 --> 07:38.541
What's he doing here?

07:39.083 --> 07:42.378
Mr. Akutayama is taking the day off
to tend to some urgent business.

07:42.462 --> 07:45.548
I'll be taking over
your Modern Japanese class today!

07:46.174 --> 07:47.300
For real?

07:47.383 --> 07:48.509
Wow!

07:49.135 --> 07:51.471
What's the matter, Asano?
You don't look so good.

07:58.060 --> 07:59.645
<i>No good.</i>

08:00.480 --> 08:04.734
<i>My eyelids... are heavier...</i>
<i>than dumbbells.</i>

08:05.443 --> 08:08.321
<i>Maybe I'll take a really short nap.</i>

08:19.457 --> 08:23.544
<i>A spy must learn to control</i>
<i>even his own sleeping patterns.</i>

08:23.628 --> 08:25.087
<i>Is that Morse code?</i>

08:26.005 --> 08:28.257
<i>By putting one half</i>
<i>of their brains to sleep,</i>

08:28.341 --> 08:31.969
<i>dolphins and migratory birds are able</i>
<i>to remain in a constant awakened state.</i>

08:32.470 --> 08:34.305
<i>This skill can be attained</i>
<i>by humans as well,</i>

08:34.388 --> 08:35.932
<i>so long as they train hard enough.</i>

08:36.432 --> 08:41.312
<i>Fact: I myself graduated</i>
<i>from total sleep at 15.</i>

08:41.395 --> 08:43.481
That means you graduated
from being a human!

08:43.940 --> 08:46.484
<i>I'll be using my threads</i>
<i>to analyze your heart rate,</i>

08:46.567 --> 08:48.694
<i>and if I detect that you're sleeping...</i>

08:49.320 --> 08:52.448
<i>Your wake-up call will be</i>
<i>a piece of chalk at the speed of sound.</i>

08:52.532 --> 08:54.158
Right, that will kill me!

08:54.617 --> 08:56.869
<i>Can't believe he's training me</i>
<i>in the middle of class.</i>

08:56.953 --> 08:59.330
<i>He's right!</i>
<i>You need to back off, Big Bro!</i>

09:00.831 --> 09:03.251
<i>You just want to torment Taiyo, don't you?</i>

09:03.334 --> 09:05.711
<i>Mutsumi! We can talk like this?</i>

09:06.212 --> 09:10.967
<i>Oh, yes. I've been</i>
<i>in a spy family for 17 years, after all.</i>

09:11.425 --> 09:13.135
<i>Really, Mutsumi!</i>

09:13.219 --> 09:15.846
<i>Starting a conversation with me</i>
<i>in code during class!</i>

09:15.930 --> 09:17.640
<i>You love your big bro too much!</i>

09:17.723 --> 09:19.559
<i>You're so adorable,</i>
<i>I want to gobble you up!</i>

09:19.642 --> 09:20.810
<i>Just kidding!</i>

09:20.893 --> 09:22.853
He's so ecstatic, it broke his brain!

09:22.937 --> 09:27.275
<i>You're beyond creepy.</i>
<i>Also, you're overworking Taiyo!</i>

09:27.358 --> 09:29.694
<i>You're just as cute</i>
<i>when you're angry, Mutsumi!</i>

09:29.777 --> 09:31.320
<i>Mutsumi? Thanks.</i>

09:31.404 --> 09:32.530
<i>I'll be all right.</i>

09:32.613 --> 09:35.825
<i>Just watch. I'm going to</i>
<i>ace this low-level training no problem!</i>

09:35.908 --> 09:39.078
<i>Hah! Wonder how many seconds</i>
<i>that bravado will last?</i>

09:47.878 --> 09:49.880
<i>Drowsiness? Fight it off!</i>

09:52.216 --> 09:54.218
You stop it right now, Big Bro!

09:54.844 --> 09:56.846
Everyone's asleep!

09:58.264 --> 10:01.017
I see you have your gas mask
on you at all times.

10:01.100 --> 10:02.727
Good for you, Mutsumi!

10:02.810 --> 10:06.480
I never dreamed
that I'd be using it against you, Big Bro!

10:07.690 --> 10:10.109
Nanao's special sleeping gas.

10:10.192 --> 10:11.986
One whiff, and you're off to dreamland!

10:13.237 --> 10:14.238
Taiyo!

10:14.864 --> 10:16.324
No, Taiyo! Wake up!

10:16.824 --> 10:19.493
Impressive that he at least
kept himself from slumping over.

10:20.119 --> 10:21.329
But it's over now!

10:26.417 --> 10:28.753
Thank goodness
you were... awake?

10:32.506 --> 10:34.508
He moved in his sleep!

10:36.177 --> 10:39.513
Looks like he's reached
the half-awake state!

10:40.556 --> 10:43.601
Just stop, will you? Are you trying
to turn Taiyo into a monster?

10:43.684 --> 10:47.146
I'm doing this all for you
and for this guy.

10:47.229 --> 10:49.440
Let's see you strive
to reach ever greater heights!

10:49.523 --> 10:50.566
Taiyo Asano!

10:56.697 --> 10:58.616
Not bad for
your first awakening!

10:58.699 --> 11:00.785
I'm going to shift into a higher gear!

11:04.330 --> 11:08.292
<i>Ugh. Taiyo's getting</i>
<i>less and less human...</i>

11:11.545 --> 11:14.548
<i>Apparently, that half-awake state</i>
<i>was a fluke,</i>

11:14.632 --> 11:16.592
<i>and it hasn't happened again since, but...</i>

11:20.721 --> 11:23.099
He's sleepwalking
all over the place again.

11:25.518 --> 11:28.020
<i>...it's left Taiyo with an odd habit.</i>

11:35.486 --> 11:36.487
YOUR TARGET IS HER HEART

11:36.570 --> 11:39.365
"Strategies for Dating,
Spy-style."

11:39.448 --> 11:42.201
SPY

11:42.284 --> 11:44.662
<i>"A spy's job is intense."</i>

11:45.955 --> 11:50.584
<i>"Are you so consumed by work that you're</i>
<i>just phoning it in with your partner?"</i>

11:52.128 --> 11:55.756
<i>"Fact: In 90% of spy marriages</i>
<i>that end in divorce,</i>

11:55.840 --> 11:59.176
<i>the cause is said to be</i>
<i>missed connections due to overwork."</i>

12:02.930 --> 12:04.640
Here you go, Taiyo.
Have some tea!

12:06.642 --> 12:08.811
-Hey, Mutsumi...
-Hmm?

12:09.395 --> 12:11.230
If you're free today...

12:13.357 --> 12:15.609
UNKNOWN NUMBER
SLIDE TO ANSWER

12:16.444 --> 12:17.445
My bad.

12:17.528 --> 12:18.904
Oh, sure.

12:18.988 --> 12:20.281
Yes, hello?

12:20.364 --> 12:22.658
<i>It's me. Mission time.</i>

12:22.742 --> 12:24.160
Mr. Hotokeyama?

12:24.243 --> 12:26.704
<i>That's right.</i>
<i>I need you to get moving right away.</i>

12:26.787 --> 12:28.664
Oh, uh...

12:29.206 --> 12:32.585
<i>I've texted you the location.</i>
<i>I'll be in touch.</i>

12:32.668 --> 12:34.128
Huh? Hey, wait.

12:36.297 --> 12:37.631
Is something wrong?

12:37.715 --> 12:40.843
Sorry. It's an urgent mission.

12:41.385 --> 12:42.595
I'll be going now!

12:43.137 --> 12:44.138
Okay.

12:44.847 --> 12:46.015
See you later!

12:50.102 --> 12:52.480
TASHIMAEN

12:52.563 --> 12:53.564
Wow!

12:53.647 --> 12:55.024
I want a balloon!

12:55.900 --> 12:57.109
<i>You're there now?</i>

12:57.193 --> 12:59.612
Yes. Uh, isn't this...

13:00.112 --> 13:02.615
<i>A male and female</i>
<i>with illicit guns</i>

13:02.698 --> 13:04.658
<i>are lurking within that amusement park.</i>

13:04.742 --> 13:06.452
<i>Smoke them out and apprehend them.</i>

13:06.911 --> 13:09.163
A couple? What do they look like?

13:09.246 --> 13:10.706
<i>I'm looking into that.</i>

13:10.790 --> 13:13.501
<i>Whatever you do, keep your eye on</i>
<i>anyone suspicious-looking.</i>

13:14.877 --> 13:16.921
Anyone suspicious-looking?

13:20.174 --> 13:22.885
Mommy, is that man all alone?

13:23.552 --> 13:25.679
<i>That would be me!</i>

13:26.847 --> 13:27.848
<i>Ugh...</i>

13:28.557 --> 13:30.601
Now, now, cheer up, will you?

13:31.268 --> 13:32.561
Thanks.

13:33.395 --> 13:35.231
Wait... Mutsumi?

13:35.314 --> 13:36.315
Oops, I came.

13:36.732 --> 13:39.401
Oops, you came? How'd you find me?

13:39.985 --> 13:42.530
-I asked Mr. Hotokeyama.
-Huh?

13:43.030 --> 13:46.242
It would look more natural for you
to be in a place like this with me, right?

13:46.325 --> 13:47.493
But it could be dangerous!

13:47.576 --> 13:49.370
Hey, keep your voice down!

13:49.453 --> 13:52.206
The couple in question
might be somewhere nearby.

13:54.166 --> 13:55.584
If you ask me...

13:56.293 --> 14:00.005
I'd say that those couples
over there seem suspicious.

14:00.089 --> 14:01.799
T-True.

14:02.258 --> 14:05.427
And at the very least,
I can defend myself.

14:05.970 --> 14:08.180
And since you're here,
I should be fine, right?

14:11.141 --> 14:14.728
<i>Well, it's not like</i>
<i>Mutsumi's the target.</i>

14:17.189 --> 14:19.525
Hey, this flavor's delicious!

14:19.608 --> 14:22.069
Come on, Taiyo! You try it, too! Here.

14:25.406 --> 14:26.407
Well?

14:27.032 --> 14:28.033
It's good.

14:28.617 --> 14:29.618
Right?

14:29.702 --> 14:30.744
<i>Hold up.</i>

14:30.828 --> 14:35.040
<i>This could be my chance</i>
<i>to show Mutsumi a good time, right?</i>

14:35.124 --> 14:36.417
Oooh!

14:37.334 --> 14:39.378
I love your outfit today, Mocchi!

14:39.461 --> 14:41.672
Not that you don't look cute
no matter what you wear!

14:41.755 --> 14:43.465
Oh, stop, Ken-Ken!

14:43.549 --> 14:44.717
Love you!

14:44.800 --> 14:46.260
-You're so sweet!
-<i>That's it!</i>

14:46.343 --> 14:47.887
-Mutsumi!
-Hmm?

14:48.387 --> 14:50.264
That outfit, it's great!

14:50.556 --> 14:53.893
I... I bet it's easy
to unleash high kicks in that!

14:59.565 --> 15:02.610
What? Oh, yes.
It's easy to move around in.

15:02.693 --> 15:04.862
You're just humoring me!

15:06.697 --> 15:09.575
Looks like one couple's
heading towards the roller coaster.

15:09.658 --> 15:11.201
ELECTRIC SHOCK
Roller Coaster

15:11.285 --> 15:12.578
Let's go after them!

15:13.287 --> 15:14.747
R-Right.

15:16.290 --> 15:17.875
I'm so scared, Ken-Ken!

15:17.958 --> 15:19.668
You'll be fine, Mocchi!

15:22.296 --> 15:23.422
Ken-Ken!

15:23.505 --> 15:24.882
Mocchi!

15:31.680 --> 15:33.641
Now, that wasn't scary at all,
was it, Mocchi?

15:33.724 --> 15:35.684
Nope! It was fun!

15:36.393 --> 15:38.729
S-Sorry, Mutsumi.

15:38.812 --> 15:41.523
After all that hard-core training,
that felt like light swaying,

15:41.607 --> 15:43.484
and I got really comfortable.

15:43.567 --> 15:45.736
Hey, it's all right! Don't worry about it!

15:47.404 --> 15:48.822
Anyway, Taiyo...

15:50.532 --> 15:54.244
Sorry. The thing is,
I can't take those scream machines.

15:54.328 --> 15:56.246
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

15:56.330 --> 15:57.790
Here, drink this.

15:59.875 --> 16:00.876
Oh...

16:01.710 --> 16:02.711
S-Sorry!

16:02.795 --> 16:04.296
N-No, I'm sorry.

16:04.380 --> 16:06.840
Looks like
they're just on a normal date.

16:06.924 --> 16:10.094
Yeah. They just look scary, I guess.

16:10.594 --> 16:12.304
That couple's next, right?

16:14.473 --> 16:15.849
<i>Two more couples left.</i>

16:15.933 --> 16:17.768
<i>We'll unmask them for sure!</i>

16:17.851 --> 16:19.895
Come on now, Mocchi!

16:19.979 --> 16:21.730
Ohh! So fast!

16:21.814 --> 16:24.066
H-How do you like it, Mutsumi?

16:24.149 --> 16:25.943
I'm having so much fun!

16:26.318 --> 16:28.654
Even though I can't see a thing!

16:28.737 --> 16:30.364
Oops, sorry!

16:32.408 --> 16:36.161
There's no centrifugal force
that can keep us apart!

16:36.620 --> 16:37.621
You're awesome!

16:38.580 --> 16:39.832
<i>Good for you!</i>

16:40.332 --> 16:41.709
Wasn't that a blast?

16:41.792 --> 16:43.043
Yeah! The best!

16:47.214 --> 16:49.091
<i>I did it again.</i>

16:49.174 --> 16:52.344
That couple seems
to be all lovey-dovey, too.

16:52.886 --> 16:54.972
What's wrong? Are you dizzy?

16:55.055 --> 16:56.557
No, I'm fine.

16:57.057 --> 16:58.350
Hey! Taiyo!

16:58.434 --> 16:59.435
Huh?

17:02.563 --> 17:03.897
One last couple.

17:04.481 --> 17:05.566
Let's go after them.

17:06.900 --> 17:08.986
Here, Mocchi! A present for you.

17:09.069 --> 17:12.239
Wow! I'm so thrilled! Thanks!

17:12.656 --> 17:14.742
Where'd that couple go?

17:15.242 --> 17:16.785
Let's search the other shops.

17:16.869 --> 17:17.870
Okay.

17:19.913 --> 17:22.291
ROSES
MAKE A GREAT GIFT!

17:33.302 --> 17:35.846
They just seem to be having tea
like any other couple.

17:35.929 --> 17:36.930
Looks like.

17:38.390 --> 17:41.018
All right,
I'm going to go get us some drinks.

17:41.101 --> 17:42.102
Okay.

17:43.479 --> 17:45.355
There's something
I'd like to show you.

17:45.856 --> 17:47.316
What would that be?

17:47.399 --> 17:49.068
It's a special-order item, you see.

17:49.151 --> 17:50.360
<i>A special-order item?</i>

17:51.153 --> 17:52.613
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

18:00.662 --> 18:02.164
A custom-made ring.

18:03.082 --> 18:04.917
Would you be so kind as to marry me?

18:05.834 --> 18:07.211
Understood.

18:10.380 --> 18:13.092
<i>I've been dragging Mutsumi around all day,</i>

18:13.175 --> 18:15.844
<i>and I can't find the couple with the gun.</i>

18:16.345 --> 18:18.180
<i>What the heck am I doing?</i>

18:19.264 --> 18:23.143
<i>I want to do something that'll make</i>
<i>Mutsumi happy, even if it's just once.</i>

18:25.187 --> 18:26.730
What the hell is your problem?

18:27.773 --> 18:30.025
Staring at that woman all this time!

18:30.109 --> 18:31.735
Huh? I wasn't looking at anyone!

18:31.819 --> 18:34.696
Who are you to talk,
making eyes at that guy!

18:34.780 --> 18:36.573
That's a load of crap, you idiot!

18:36.657 --> 18:38.158
What did you say, ugly face?

18:38.242 --> 18:40.410
<i>But they were so close</i>
<i>that it was obnoxious.</i>

18:40.869 --> 18:42.913
Damn, I've had enough of you.

18:42.996 --> 18:44.873
Right back at ya, bastard!

18:44.957 --> 18:48.585
Any blemish on my life
gets rubbed out instantly!

18:48.669 --> 18:51.797
<i>Engraved! It's a custom-made gun!</i>

18:52.256 --> 18:55.884
I was a moron
for being with someone like you!

18:56.385 --> 18:57.845
Run!

19:00.222 --> 19:02.724
What? Hey! Taiyo!

19:09.189 --> 19:10.190
Damn.

19:13.110 --> 19:14.778
Cover your ears tight!

19:28.667 --> 19:29.668
Hey!

19:29.751 --> 19:30.752
What?

19:30.836 --> 19:31.879
Take a hike, outsider!

19:39.845 --> 19:42.139
Take your lovers' spat somewhere else!

19:43.473 --> 19:46.351
METROPOLITAN POLICE

19:47.311 --> 19:48.312
No way!

19:48.395 --> 19:51.523
I didn't get to watch
the sunset with Ken-Ken yet!

19:51.607 --> 19:53.525
Ken-Ken! Ken-Ken!

19:54.193 --> 19:55.777
Come on, give me a break!

19:57.696 --> 19:59.615
It's just a little longer, you know!

20:00.115 --> 20:01.200
Tightwad!

20:01.283 --> 20:03.035
Mocchi!

20:04.786 --> 20:09.082
For crying out loud. Can't tell
if those two are on good terms or bad.

20:11.084 --> 20:13.378
Anyway, good job today.

20:13.962 --> 20:15.088
I owe you one.

20:15.797 --> 20:19.801
<i>So that was a smile after all.</i>

20:22.554 --> 20:28.393
<i>H-H-He sent him</i>
<i>to an amusement park with Mutsumi?</i>

20:30.145 --> 20:32.356
-Mutsumi!
-Hmm?

20:32.439 --> 20:33.565
Unforgivable!

20:33.649 --> 20:36.360
-I'm hungry.
-Unforgivable! Taiyo Asano!

20:47.871 --> 20:51.458
Well, talk about a rough day, huh?

20:51.541 --> 20:53.210
I-I guess so!

20:53.710 --> 20:56.088
At least we got to
buy souvenirs for everyone

20:56.171 --> 20:58.340
and take in all the attractions
after that went down!

20:58.799 --> 21:02.761
Come to think of it, why did you
want to ride the Ferris wheel last?

21:02.844 --> 21:04.346
Huh? Oh, uh...

21:04.429 --> 21:06.098
Because, see...

21:06.181 --> 21:10.269
couples who see the sunset
from this Ferris wheel get to...

21:10.769 --> 21:12.521
they get to live happily ever after.

21:14.606 --> 21:17.234
S-So that's what this is about, huh?

21:20.445 --> 21:21.947
Listen, Mutsumi.

21:24.283 --> 21:25.284
Here.

21:28.453 --> 21:30.872
It got like this in that shootout,

21:30.956 --> 21:34.710
but the flower itself isn't too messed up,
and it would be a shame to toss it.

21:35.377 --> 21:39.589
Today, I wanted to show you a good time
for once to thank you for all that you do.

21:40.674 --> 21:43.302
But in the end,
I couldn't do anything for you.

21:46.513 --> 21:47.514
Mutsumi?

21:47.973 --> 21:49.975
Huh? Oh, uh...

21:50.517 --> 21:53.895
I never thought you were the type
to do this kind of thing, Taiyo,

21:53.979 --> 21:56.231
so I was a little surprised...

22:01.153 --> 22:03.655
I'm so happy. Thanks!

22:08.035 --> 22:13.165
No, thank you... for everything.

23:47.968 --> 23:50.887
NEXT TIME
BUG
